<!--
  Quick Settings tile icon.

  🔴 The fill stays SOLID WHITE and that is not an oversight of the design
  pass. SystemUI re-tints a tile icon from the shade's own palette (and inverts
  it between the tile's active/inactive states), so a brand colour here is
  discarded on an inactive tile and fights the shade on an active one. The same
  drawable is the notification small icon, where the platform also hard-tints
  from Notification.Builder.setColor() — which is where Dicta's accent is
  applied instead (see BubbleService.buildNotification()).

  The path data is the same glyph as ic_mic.xml, so the tile, the bubble and
  the launcher icon are one mark in three tint contexts.
-->
